--! The browser platform (`docs/design/boundary.md` §9.1; `backend.md`
--! §15.11): a page program, and the `dom` markup lowering that compiles a
--! view into templates the page clones and patches.
--!
--! `Program` is data: `program` returns the record it is given, and the
--! platform's runtime is the only code that reads it. It renders `view
--! init` into `document.body`, and every message a handler sends goes
--! through `update`; the page renders the new model once, on one microtask
--! after the messages of a task, writing only the holes whose values
--! changed.
import Html exposing (Html)


--| What `main` is: a page program.
pub foreign type Program


--| A page with a model: `init` is rendered first, and every message a
--| handler sends goes through `update` before the next render.
pub foreign program : { init : model, update : msg, model -> model, view : model -> Html msg } -> Program
